GAL22V10
UA6RHWR

AB1 AB2 AB3 AB4 AB5 AB6 GALSTB RCFG8 RCFG4 RCFG2 BASEA GND
RW CFGIN NC15 ACPHASE RST DB15 DB14 DB13 DB12 NC22 DRVEN VCC

; =====================================================================
; UA6 - RocHard RH800C  -  ua6_hd + WRITE-RELEASE /_DRVEN  (RAM bring-up)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; IDENTICAL to ua6_hd.pld EXCEPT the /_DRVEN equation.
;
; WHY (LA-confirmed 2026-08-01, roctec_ram_cfgd_trace.csv):
;   With the RAM strap set, the card RED-SCREENS because /_RAMCE (U11.22,
;   = U2 data-buffer enable) fires at $F8xxxx (motherboard Kickstart ROM)
;   -> U2 fights the Kickstart ROM on D8-15 -> corrupt fetch -> red.
;   Mechanism (chained cracked fusemaps):
;     /_RAMCE (U11 o22) = /BASE_B & _UDS & not-RST         (no A20 term!)
;     /BASE_B (U12 o18) = /_LATCH_EN & /_GALSTROBE
;     /_GALSTROBE (UA4 o21) strap terms ride on /GALCLK1 (UA4 o19), which
;       decodes region by A21..A23 + straps + the latched base o16/o17/o18
;       and NEVER checks A16-A20 -> can't tell $E8 from $F8.
;   Its one region-7 term (line 37) needs o16 & o17 & o18 = 1,1,1.
;   LA proved: at the $F8 fire, o16.o17.o18 (CFGD12/14/13) = 1,1,1.
;
; ROOT CAUSE: o16/o17/o18 are UA4 SELF-HOLDING latches (o=o), oe=/_DRVEN.
;   ua6_hd pins /_DRVEN LOW forever -> UA4's oe never releases -> the
;   latches never CAPTURE a defined base, they settle to 111 and hold ->
;   the region-7 term stays armed for all of $E0-$FF incl $F8.
;
; THE FIX UNDER TEST: release /_DRVEN during WRITES (add & RW). During the
;   autoconfig base WRITE (R/W=0) the card needn't drive data, so /_DRVEN
;   can go high, UA4 releases o16/o17/o18, the written base (which has a 0
;   bit) reaches /_CFGDxx via the 32.7R resistors, and the next read
;   re-asserts /_DRVEN latching a non-111 base -> region-7 term disarmed
;   -> no $F8 fire.  BLUNT first cut: this releases on EVERY write (incl
;   IDE) -> may need narrowing to config offset $48 via AB1-6 if it
;   destabilises. VERIFY on the LA: CFGD12/14/13 should stop reading 111,
;   and /_RAMCE must NOT fire at region 1111 ($F8).  Also confirm the HD
;   still ENUMERATES (DiagROM shows the Z2 board) - reburn ua6_hd if not.
;
; BOARD SETTINGS (RAM bring-up): game II - DIP-1 ON - DIP-2 ON -
;   JPA1 = 2M - SIMM0+SIMM1 (bank 0) fitted, or empty for a pure
;   logic-contention re-check.
; =====================================================================


; ---- /_DRVEN (pin 23) : latched, but RELEASES ON WRITES -------------
; ua6_hd was: /DRVEN = /CFGIN & /BASEA & RST + /CFGIN & /DRVEN & RST
; Add & RW to both terms so /_DRVEN deasserts (high) on any write,
; letting UA4 capture the autoconfig base into o16/o17/o18.
/DRVEN = /CFGIN & /BASEA & RW & RST
       + /CFGIN & /DRVEN & RW & RST


; ---- /_AC_PHASE (pin 16) -> U11.5 : LEAVE UNDRIVEN (Hi-Z) -----------
; Unchanged from ua6_hd. Driving it LOW red-screened during HD bring-up;
; LA later proved static levels here don't affect the RAM fault. Hi-Z.
ACPHASE.T = VCC
ACPHASE.E = AB1 & /AB1


; ---- DB12-15 (pins 18-21) : permanent Hi-Z (unchanged) --------------
; Let the boot ROM (U6/U20) drive the controller er_Type. UA6 does NOT
; announce RAM here - RAM usability is handled separately (AddMemList).
DB15.T = VCC
DB15.E = AB1 & /AB1
DB14.T = VCC
DB14.E = AB1 & /AB1
DB13.T = VCC
DB13.E = AB1 & /AB1
DB12.T = VCC
DB12.E = AB1 & /AB1


; ---- NC15 (pin 15), NC22 (pin 22) : unconnected pads, Hi-Z ----------
NC15.T = VCC
NC15.E = AB1 & /AB1
NC22.T = VCC
NC22.E = AB1 & /AB1


DESCRIPTION

UA6 HD-bring-up clone with WRITE-RELEASE /_DRVEN for RocHard RH800C.

Identical to ua6_hd.pld except /_DRVEN gains an "& RW" gate on both its
set and hold terms, so it deasserts on writes. Purpose: let UA4 capture a
defined (non-all-1s) autoconfig base into its o16/o17/o18 latches during
the base write, so UA4's /GALCLK1 region-7 term (line 37, needs
o16.o17.o18=111) stops arming and /_GALSTROBE / /_RAMCE no longer fire at
$F8xxxx (Kickstart), which was the strap-on red-screen.

FIRST TEST BURN - blunt (releases on all writes). If it destabilises
(oscillation on /_DRVEN<->/_E8WIN, or HD stops enumerating), narrow the
release to config offset 0x48 using AB1-6, or revert to ua6_hd.

TEST (LA, channel map as roctec_ram_cfgd_trace):
  1. HD still enumerates? (DiagROM one Z2 board, mfr 2144).
  2. Strap ON: does CFGD12/14/13 stop reading 111?
  3. Strap ON: does /_RAMCE STILL fire at region 1111 ($F8)?  It must NOT.
